; individual external verification not claimed","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0106","relatedNodeIds":["FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0106"],"fingerprint":"1cd168b29a5afc544ffc","semanticKey101":"580006eea7bd84c9f1d5765e0d0d8432b8892e990dbf0efe070df047c1581bb5","editorialRevision101":"specific factual/distractor/duplicate correction","practiceRepetitionKeys95":["FACT:ARCHED-NEW101-0106"],"testedRelation95":"v101:e0710222d4c2bc77ed9c"},{"id":"ARCHED-NEW101-0107","qid":1010107,"major":"History & Politics","stem":"After the revocation of the Edict of Nantes, many Huguenots:","choices":["Established the English monarchy","Emigrated from France","Founded the Jesuit order","Formed the Roman Senate","Restored the Byzantine Empire"],"answer":"Emigrated from France","correctIndex":1,"explanation":"The revocation led many French Protestants to leave for other European states and overseas settlements.","group":"Early modern Europe","topic74":"Early modern Europe","format":"context_relation","skill74":"context_relation","task101":"context_relation","examLanguages":["en","it"],"scope":"shared","editorialStatus74":"ready","reviewStatus":"editorially_reviewed","publication_ready":true,"previewOnly95":false,"version":"editorial-v101","difficulty74":"unrated","references":[],"evidenceStatus101":"editorial factual review; individual external verification not claimed","nodeId":"FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0107","relatedNodeIds":["FACT101-ARCHED-NEW101-0107"],"fingerprint":"a8e78a73dd386c1f0da0","semanticKey101":"0afeb21df000b3f71002f73efdad49d989959e48f63698f1e2db06bcc33510aa","editorialRevision101":"specific factual/distractor/duplicate correction","practiceRepetitionKeys95":["FACT:ARCHED-NEW101-0107"],"testedRelation95":"v101:72fb6ac8711ba4bda41b"},{"id":"ARCHED-NEW101-0108","qid":1010108,"major":"History & Politics","stem":"The Pragmatic Sanction issued by Charles VI sought to secure the succession of:","choices":["Catherine II","Mary Stuart","Elizabeth I","Christina of Sweden","Maria Theresa"]